    {
      "heading": "Seventh, just behind sixth",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-grigoriy-zatravkin-identity-0",
        "person-grigoriy-zatravkin-roster-0"
      ],
      "text": "The entry named Grigoriy Zatravkin reaches seventh on the ARC-AGI-3 public board at 45.02. Its recorded morning score event moves from 40.63 and eleventh place to 45.02 and seventh: a 4.39-point improvement that leaves it just 0.09 behind sixth-placed 復活の混テキスト. The fresh roster lists grigoriyzatravkin and florenciasolange. This is a team result; the two-account observation does not assign responsibility for the gain."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fifth closes on fourth",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Son & Mark & Ronen improves from 47.25 to 48.92 overnight but stays fifth. The last dance holds fourth at 49.85, leaving a gap of 0.93; mtg remains third at 50.37. The advance compresses the chase without changing its leading order. Zatravkin’s move further down the top ten pushes unchanged Majkel1337 to eighth, NVARC3 to ninth and artificialagencylab.com to tenth."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The leading pair stays clear",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-16-2000-arc-3-fukkatsu-team-rises-to-sixth"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs leads at 68.91 and Yi-Chia Chen follows at 67.49, both unchanged against the midnight comparison. Chen remains more than seventeen points ahead of third. The wire’s report of 復活の混テキスト reaching sixth belongs to the preceding day’s advance; its 45.11 is unchanged overnight. The provisional gold score also holds at 38.20. Farther down, Muurur gains 1.29 points and 140 places against the edition baseline to reach 130th at 32.76. Public medal positions remain provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Research beyond the standings",
      "sourceIds": [
        "social-2111278061039800629"
      ],
      "text": "Kevin Patrick Murphy says his forthcoming Boston ARC talk will cover his Model Discovery Agent and a proposed scientific benchmark inspired by ARC-AGI-3. Agents would choose experiments in a partially observed, noisy simulator, build a causal model and be judged on predictions for new interventions. The proposal makes experimental choice and prediction the test; it is an upcoming talk, not a released benchmark or a new Kaggle score."
    },
